 4. O-O {White castles and asks Black to commit. Against ...c6 the plan is d3 and Nbd2 for e4, or b3 and c4 to hit d5 from the side.}
 4... Bg4 {[%cal Gg4f3] Active development. The bishop on g4 controls f5 and e6.}
 5. d3 {Prepares e4. Supports the centre: the pawn on d3 controls c4 and e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1.}
 5... Nbd7 {Supports ...e5. Develops the knight to d7, where it controls e5.}
 6. Nbd2 {Supports e4. Develops the knight to d2, where it controls e4.}
 6... e5 {Black's ideal centre. The pawn on e5 controls d4 and f4. It also opens a line for the bishop on f8.}
 7. e4 {[%cal Ge4d5] Challenges it immediately. Claims the centre: the pawn on e4 controls f5 and eyes the pawn on d5.}
 7... dxe4 {Black releases the tension and opens the d-file.}
