 4. O-O {White castles. The f5-bishop is Black's best piece, so look for d3 and Nbd2 followed by e4 to blunt it, or Nh4 to chase it.}
 4... e6 {Black has a London-style setup. Supports the centre: the pawn on e6 supports the pawn on d5 and the bishop on f5. It also opens a line for the bishop on f8.}
 5. d3 {[%csl Ge4] Prepares Nbd2 and e4, hitting the f5-bishop. Supports the centre: the pawn on d3 controls c4 and e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1.}
 5... h6 {Makes a retreat square on h7. The pawn on h6 controls g5.}
 6. Nbd2 {Supports e4. Develops the knight to d2, where it controls e4.}
 6... Be7 {A modest but safe home for the bishop: it shields the f6-knight from pins and lets Black castle next. Don't worry that it looks passive; it can reroute later.}
