12. Bf4 {[%cal Gf4e5] Defends the e5 wedge and supports the attack.} *

[Event "vs 1...Nf6"]

{Against 1...Nf6, White can play c4 (Réti/English) or g3 (KIA style). Both keep the game in the hypermodern style.}
1. Nf3 {[%csl Ge5,Gd4] A flexible start. Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and d4.}
1... Nf6 {Black mirrors White, keeping the game flexible.}
2. c4 {[%cal Gc4d5] Controls d5 and heads into English/Réti territory.}
(2. g3 {[%cal Gf1g2] The KIA route. The pawn on g3 controls f4 and h4.}
