 3... Bg7 {Black contests the long diagonal. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
 4. O-O {White castles and waits. In double-fianchetto positions the first side to strike the centre with a pawn (d4 or c4 here) usually gets the better version.}
 4... O-O {Black castles too. Now White chooses: c4 and d4 for space, or d3 and e4 to aim for a King's Indian Attack type game.}
 5. d3 {Prepares e4. Supports the centre: the pawn on d3 controls c4 and e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1.}
