[Event "vs 1...d5: 2.g3 ...Bf5 setups"]

{When Black develops the bishop to f5 early, White targets b7 with c4, cxd5 and Qb3.}
1. Nf3 {[%csl Ge5,Gd4] A flexible start. Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and d4.}
1... d5 {Black takes the centre. The pawn on d5 controls c4 and e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c8 and the queen on d8.}
2. g3 {Fianchetto. The pawn on g3 controls f4 and h4.}
2... Bf5 {The bishop develops early. The bishop on f5 controls e4.}
3. Bg2 {Fianchetto. The bishop on g2 rakes the long diagonal through f3. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
3... e6 {A London-style setup. Supports the centre: the pawn on e6 supports the pawn on d5 and the bishop on f5. It also opens a line for the queen on d8 and the bishop on f8.}
4. O-O {White castles. The f5-bishop is Black's pride; White's d3, Nbd2 and e4 aim to blunt it.}
4... Nf6 {Black develops toward e4. White's plan: d3 and Nbd2, then e4.}
5. d3 {Prepares e4. Supports the centre: the pawn on d3 controls c4 and e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1.}
5... h6 {Makes a retreat square on h7. The pawn on h6 controls g5.}
6. c4 {Challenges d5. Supports the centre: the pawn on c4 controls b5 and eyes the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1.}
6... c6 {Supports d5. Supports the centre: the pawn on c6 controls b5 and supports the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
7. cxd5 {Opens the c-file. Takes the pawn on d5; Black will want to recapture.}
7... exd5 {The bishop on f5 now leaves b7 unguarded. Recaptures on d5, restoring the material balance.}
8. Nc3 {White develops, pressuring d5. The Carlsbad structure means minority attack ideas with b4–b5.}
8... Be7 {A modest but safe home for the bishop: it shields the f6-knight from pins and lets Black castle next. Don't worry that it looks passive; it can reroute later.}
9. Qb3 {[%cal Gb3b7] Attacks b7, which the f5-bishop left behind. The queen goes to b3 and eyes the pawn on d5.}
9... Qb6 {The queen goes to b6 and controls d4. White's last move put a queen on b3, which this now pressures.}
10. Be3 {Development with tempo on the queen. The bishop on e3 controls d4. It attacks the queen on b6.} *

